  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Claude Code workspace: browser verification is now part of the normal workflow. After a change that is visible on screen, Claude Code starts the development server itself when the design workspace lives inside a host solution (dotnet run in the background; the URL is taken from the host's CLAUDE.md / launchSettings.json and remembered in LocalEnvironment.md), deploys its edits with the designer's headless deploy, logs in and checks the page with Playwright, and stops a server it started. The generated .claude/settings.local.json (design workspace and host root) therefore also allows dotnet run, node, npm install and npx playwright. BrowserTestGuide.md was rewritten around this flow (server start, deploy, login, DOM-based checks).\n- The headless deploy is gated by the new DeployInfo.AllowCliDeploy setting of designer 1.3.32 (any deploy method; false is refused by the CLI), and the workspace rules describe it as the safety boundary, like AllowCliSqlAccess for sql. The bundled templates mark their local deploy target as allowed.",
